<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Olmsted returns with his caregiver about six months after his first visit, twelve weeks after donepezil was increased to 10 mg each morning. He has had no nausea, diarrhea, dizziness, fainting, or vivid dreams, and his appetite is good. His memory is unchanged by his caregiver&apos;s account, and he enjoys the adult day program two days a week for its gardens. He has had no falls, no wandering, and no night-time confusion. His caregiver finished the education program, sleeps better, and has two free days a week. They went through the home safety checklist together this month: knob covers on the stove, locked medicines, and night lights on the way to the bathroom. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Medicine</td><td>Donepezil 10 mg for twelve weeks; no side effects</td></tr><tr><td>Course</td><td>Memory unchanged; no new behavioral symptoms</td></tr><tr><td>Safety</td><td>No falls or wandering; home safety checklist completed</td></tr><tr><td>Caregiver</td><td>Education program completed; adult day program two days a week</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

