    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Mild dementia, type undetermined (F03.A0)</content>. Stable clinically at CDR 1 on donepezil 10 mg, with heart rate 60, no fainting, and stable weight. Mood better (PHQ-9 4, from 6). Home safety and caregiver support in place. [S]<list><item>Continue donepezil 10 mg each morning.</item><item>Next dementia review in about three months, and the yearly review at one year from diagnosis with MoCA, ADL and IADL, CDR stage, and the Zarit Burden Interview.</item><item>Yearly behavioral neurology review, or sooner with a faster decline, new behavioral symptoms, or falls.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Medication review with the AGS Beers Criteria (anticholinergic burden, sedatives, sleeping pills, antipsychotics)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No anticholinergic, sedating, or other Beers-list drugs</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Neuropsychiatric symptom screen (NPI-Q)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Mild apathy only; no hallucinations, agitation, wandering, or sleep disturbance</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Cholinesterase inhibitor tolerability and benefit: heart rate, fainting, nausea, diarrhea, weight, sleep and dreams</td><td>Each follow-up on treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>On 10 mg for twelve weeks: heart rate 60, no fainting, no gastrointestinal effects, weight stable at 71.0 kg, no vivid dreams; stable course</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Antipsychotic appropriateness and taper review</td><td>Every visit if on an antipsychotic</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Not on an antipsychotic</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Vascular risk-factor control (blood pressure, lipids, glucose, smoking)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Blood pressure 130/76 mmHg; LDL 118 mg/dL and statin decision at the wellness visit; never smoked</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Home safety evaluation</td><td>At diagnosis and each follow-up</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Checklist reviewed: stove knob covers, locked medicines, night lights; the review missed at three months is now done</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Cognitive test (MoCA)</td><td>Annually; every visit if a change is reported</td><td>Up to date</td><td>MoCA 19 six months ago; no change reported; due at the yearly review</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>ADL (Katz) and IADL (Lawton-Brody)</td><td>Annually, and at any reported change</td><td>Up to date</td><td>No change reported; due at the yearly review</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Dementia stage (CDR or FAST)</td><td>Annually</td><td>Up to date</td><td>CDR 1; due at the yearly review</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Depression screen (PHQ-9)</td><td>Annually, and at any reported change</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-9 4, down from 6; no thoughts of self-harm</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Fall-risk assessment (Timed Up and Go, gait and balance)</td><td>Annually</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Timed Up and Go 11 seconds six weeks ago; no falls</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Driving safety (CDR-based)</td><td>At diagnosis and annually</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Not driving</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Firearms, wandering, and financial safety</td><td>At diagnosis and with any change</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No firearms; bracelet worn; no wandering; finances overseen</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Caregiver burden (Zarit Burden Interview) and caregiver needs</td><td>At diagnosis, then every 6 to 12 months</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Zarit 24 three months ago; caregiver sleeping better with two free days a week; repeat at the yearly review</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Advance care planning and goals of care</td><td>At diagnosis, then annually and at stage changes</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Recorded three months ago and reviewed at the wellness visit</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>TSH, vitamin B12, blood count, and metabolic panel</td><td>At diagnosis; repeat only with acute cognitive worsening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Normal at diagnosis; no acute change</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Syphilis and HIV testing</td><td>Only with risk factors or atypical features</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>No risk factors</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Structural brain MRI, non-contrast</td><td>Once at diagnosis; repeat only with an atypical course or focal change</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Done once at diagnosis</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Amyloid or tau biomarkers (blood, CSF, or amyloid PET) and APOE genotype</td><td>Before anti-amyloid therapy, or when the result would change care</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Declined; no change in his wishes</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Anti-amyloid antibody therapy with ARIA surveillance MRI</td><td>Only if anti-amyloid therapy is started</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Not chosen</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Lifestyle: aerobic exercise about twice a week, hearing, vision, sleep, social engagement</td><td>Ongoing</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Daily walks and the adult day program; hearing normal at the wellness visit; eye examination still to be booked</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Dementia care navigation and caregiver support program</td><td>At enrollment, with ongoing support</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Education program completed; adult day program two days a week</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Vaccination status (influenza, pneumococcal, zoster, COVID-19, Tdap)</td><td>Yearly, per the CDC schedule</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Influenza, PCV20, and zoster dose 1 at the wellness visit; zoster dose 2 and Tdap due in the next four months</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Complete the reversible-cause tests and brain MRI and discuss the diagnosis with him and his caregiver by the four-week visit. Outcome by 2026-06-02: Tests and MRI showed no reversible cause; diagnosis of mild dementia of undetermined type discussed with both [S]</item><item>A safety plan in place by the three-month review: no driving, medicines supervised, finances overseen, and medical identification worn. Outcome by 2026-08-04: Stopped driving after the consultation; caregiver gives medicines from a weekly organizer and oversees bill paying with his agreement; medical identification bracelet worn [S]</item><item>Donepezil at 10 mg daily without side effects and with resting heart rate 55 or above by the six-month review. Outcome by 2026-10-27: On 10 mg for three months; heart rate 60; no nausea, diarrhea, weight loss, or vivid dreams [S]</item><item>Caregiver burden assessed and support in place by the six-month review. Outcome by 2026-10-27: Zarit Burden Interview 24 at three months; caregiver education program completed and two days a week of adult day program begun [S]</item><item>Name a health care agent and record his values and wishes while he can take full part, by the three-month review. Outcome by 2026-08-04: Health care agent named and his wishes recorded at the three-month review [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Practice parameter: diagnosis of dementia (an evidence-based review). Report of the Quality Standards Subcommittee of the American Academy of Neurology (2001); Alzheimer&apos;s Association clinical practice guideline for the Diagnostic Evaluation, Testing, Counseling, and Disclosure of Suspected Alzheimer&apos;s Disease and Related Disorders (DETeCD-ADRD): Executive summary of recommendations for primary care (2025); American Geriatrics Society 2023 updated AGS Beers Criteria for potentially inappropriate medication use in older adults (2023); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, Non-Alzheimer&apos;s dementia and Alzheimer&apos;s disease monographs (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Dementia review in about three months; yearly review with MoCA, ADL and IADL, CDR stage, and the Zarit Burden Interview at one year from diagnosis. Second zoster dose and Tdap within the next four months. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
